---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';
---
<SiteLayout
  title="AgentX — The open source AI coding agent"
  description="AgentX is an open source AI coding agent for terminal-first software development."
>
  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="shell hero-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="kicker">OPEN SOURCE · TERMINAL FIRST</p>
          <h1>The AI coding agent for the whole repository.</h1>
          <p class="hero-lead">AgentX reads the project, turns requests into a plan, makes focused changes, and verifies the result from the same terminal workflow.</p>
          <div class="actions">
            <a class="button" href="/docs/installation/">Install AgentX</a>
            <a class="secondary" href="/docs/intro/">Read the docs →</a>
          </div>
          <p class="proof">Works with hosted providers and local models. Built for real software projects.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="terminal" aria-label="AgentX terminal preview">
          <div class="term-top"><span>~/workspace/agentx</span><span>agentx</span></div>
          <div class="term-body">
            <div>$ agentx</div>
            <div class="muted">Reading repository structure…</div>
            <div class="muted">Checking package scripts…</div>
            <div class="term-line"></div>
            <div>Plan</div>
            <div class="plan"><span>01</span>Inspect affected files</div>
            <div class="plan"><span>02</span>Implement the smallest change</div>
            <div class="plan"><span>03</span>Run project checks</div>
            <div class="plan"><span>04</span>Report what changed</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="tagline">
      <div class="shell">
        <h2>Understand first. Change precisely. Verify everything.</h2>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div>
            <p class="kicker">WHY AGENTX</p>
            <h2>A coding agent that stays close to the code.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>AgentX is designed for developers who want agentic speed without losing visibility into the repository, commands, and final diff.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="benefits">
          <article class="benefit"><span>01</span><h3>Repository-aware</h3><p>Inspect source, configuration, dependencies, and project conventions before editing.</p></article>
          <article class="benefit"><span>02</span><h3>Plan-first</h3><p>Turn a request into explicit steps so the intended work is clear before execution begins.</p></article>
          <article class="benefit"><span>03</span><h3>Terminal-native</h3><p>Keep the workflow where developers already build, test, search, and ship software.</p></article>
          <article class="benefit"><span>04</span><h3>Verification built in</h3><p>Run the checks that matter, inspect failures, and iterate instead of stopping at a generated patch.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="dark">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div>
            <p class="kicker">THE WORKFLOW</p>
            <h2>One loop from request to verified change.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>Designed to make agent activity legible rather than magical.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="loop">
          <div class="loop-row"><span>01</span><h3>Plan</h3><p>Define the outcome, constraints, and affected areas.</p></div>
          <div class="loop-row"><span>02</span><h3>Read</h3><p>Inspect the repository and understand how the current system works.</p></div>
          <div class="loop-row"><span>03</span><h3>Execute</h3><p>Use the terminal and project tools to make focused changes.</p></div>
          <div class="loop-row"><span>04</span><h3>Verify</h3><p>Run tests, type checks, builds, or other checks relevant to the change.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="editorial">
      <div class="shell two-col">
        <div>
          <p class="kicker">OPEN &amp; FLEXIBLE</p>
          <h2>Use the models and workflow that fit your project.</h2>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p>Connect a supported hosted provider or keep inference closer to your own environment with a local model setup.</p>
          <a class="arrow" href="/docs/providers/">Explore model providers →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="install">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div>
            <p class="kicker">GET STARTED</p>
            <h2>Put AgentX in your terminal.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>Install the CLI, open a repository, and start with a concrete outcome.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="install-box">
          <code>npm i -g @agent-qofeno/agentx-cli@latest</code>
          <button type="button" data-copy="npm i -g @agent-qofeno/agentx-cli@latest">Copy</button>
        </div>
        <div class="faq">
          <details><summary>Where should I start? <span>+</span></summary><p>Install AgentX, open your project directory, and use the Introduction to understand the four-step workflow.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Can I use local models? <span>+</span></summary><p>Yes. See the Local models guide for supported local inference workflows.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Where are the commands documented? <span>+</span></summary><p>Use the Commands page for session controls and shortcuts.</p></details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cta">
      <div class="shell cta-inner">
        <div>
          <p class="kicker">AGENTX</p>
          <h2>Build with context, not guesswork.</h2>
          <p>Read the repository. Plan the work. Make the change. Verify it.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="button-light" href="/docs/installation/">Install AgentX</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <script>
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-copy]').forEach((button) => {
      button.addEventListener('click', async () => {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(button.dataset.copy || '');
        button.textContent = 'Copied';
        setTimeout(() => { button.textContent = 'Copy'; }, 1400);
      });
    });
  </script>
</SiteLayout>
